		- Part C: I calculated the center of each histogram bin using bin_centers = (bins[:-1] + bins[1:]) / 2. I then evaluated the theoretical Gaussian distribution at each of these bin centers using (P(x)=[1/(sigma*sqrt{2pi})]exp[-(x-mu)^2/(2*sigma^2)]). Because this equation gives a probability density while the histogram represents the number of draws in each bin, I multiplied the Gaussian values by N = 10000 to obtain the expected number of draws. Since the histogram bin width was 1, no additional numerical bin-width scaling was necessary. I plotted these expected counts over the histogram using plt.plot() and saved the resulting figure as another PNG file. The theoretical Gaussian curve followed the overall shape of the randomly generated histogram and was centered near the specified mean of 55.


